so to provide some opening remarks to  the conference we're pleased to have dr.  John crystal the chair of the department  of psychiatry here at Yale and the  Robert L McNeil junior professor of  translational research and professor of  Neurobiology he's also the chief of  psychiatry at yeaah new haven hospital  and director of several research centers  here at you please joining me in  welcoming dr. crystal it's a pleasure on  behalf of the department of psychiatry  and the medical school here at yale to  welcome all of you to our community this  is a very special conference that we've  come to look forward to every year and I  want to thank Emily and Seth and the  national education alliance for  borderline personality disorder dr.  Hoffman who's who has been very  important critical to this conference to  to bring this conference to Yale into  our community borderline personality  disorder is a is a very problematic very  misunderstood and vary from a clinical  perspective very challenging disorder so  I I'm thrilled to see this wonderful set  of presentations and discussions that  will help to advance our thinking in our  ability to help people and families  where people have borderline personality  disorder you know in our in this state  and in this time we can't but help be  reminded about how active we have to be  in advocating for people with mental  illness that they should be able to get  access to the help and services that  they need and that there be support for  research to advance the state of the  knowledge about both about understanding  the problems and developing new ways to  treat these problems in our state we  we've been dealing with the state budget  and the  impact of that on potentially on the  access to care and the and research  support so being coming together in this  in this kind of context is not only a  reminder about how the people who are  suffering need to be able to get access  to the support that they need but how  actively we all have to be to ensure  that that access can continue in the  current context so this is a wonderful  conference we're so thrilled that you  all can come together to work on this  very important problem and I hope you  have a wonderful day thank you
 

